ter the JSON.\n\n## Input JSON structure\n\nThe input is FLAT except where shown nested below. Note in particular that\n\"Other Interest\" and \"EPF Taxable Interest\" are two separate top-level numbers:\n\"Other Interest\" is NOT an object and does NOT contain \"EPF Taxable Interest\".\n\n- \"Age\": number\n- \"Employment Type\": string          (\"private\" | \"government\")\n- \"Tax Regime\": string               (\"old\" | \"new\") -- USE THE REGIME GIVEN; do not pick the cheaper one\n- \"City\": string                     (\"metro\" | \"non-metro\")\n- \"Gross Salary\": { \"Basic Salary\", \"Dearness Allowance\", \"HRA\", \"Conveyance Allowance\",\n                    \"Medical Allowance\", \"Bonuses and Incentives\", \"Overtime Pay\",\n                    \"LTA\", \"Special Allowance\", \"Entertainment Allowance\" }  -- all numbers\n- \"Actual Rent Paid\", \"LTA Travel Expenses Claimed\", \"Professional Tax\": numbers\n- \"Stock Sale Transactions\": [ { \"Sale Price\", \"Cost Price\", \"Quantity\", \"Brokerage\", \"STT\",\n                                 \"Purchase Date\", \"Sale Date\", \"FMV as of 31 Jan 2018\" } ]\n- \"Long Term Capital Loss\", \"Short Term Capital Loss\": [ { \"Financial Year\", \"Loss Amount\" } ]\n- \"Mutual Fund Transactions\": [ { \"Type\", \"Purchase Date\", \"Sale Date\",\n                                  \"Purchase Value\", \"Sale Value\" } ]\n- \"Privately Owned Vehicle\", \"Bonds\", \"Debentures\", \"G-Secs\":\n      each { \"Sale Amount\", \"Purchase Amount\", \"Held for duration in years\" }\n- \"Savings Bank Interest\": number\n- \"Deposit Interest\": number\n- \"Other Interest\": number           <-- a plain amount, not a container\n- \"EPF Taxable Interest\": number     <-- a sibling of the above, not nested inside it\n- \"PPF\", \"ELSS\", \"NSC\", \"Sukanya Samriddhi Yojana\", \"SCSS\": numbers\n- \"EPF\": { \"Employee Contribution\": { \"Deducted from Salary\", \"Voluntary\" },\n           \"Employer Contribution\" }\n- \"Pension Scheme Premium\": { \"Amount\", \"Number of Years Paid\" }\n- \"NPS\": { \"Tier-1 Self Contribution\", \"Tier-1 Employer Contribution\", \"Tier-2\" }\n- \"Education Loan Interest\": { \"Interest Paid\", \"Year of Repayment\" }\n- \"Health Insurance\": [ { \"Payment Purpose\", \"Number of Years Paid\", \"Beneficiary\",\n                          \"Beneficiary Age\", \"Paid By\", \"Payment Mode\", \"Amount\" } ]\n- \"Donations\": [ { \"Scheme Name\", \"Amount\", \"Mode\" } ]\n- \"TDS\": number\n\nUse the values exactly as given. Do not substitute a statutory default for a\ndeclared figure, even when the declared figure is 0.\n\n## Input field interpretation\n\nThese clarify the semantics of certain input fields \u2014 they are NOT tax rules:\n\n- \"FMV as of 31 Jan 2018\": Fair Market Value of the stock on 31-Jan-2018.\n- \"Pension Scheme Premium \u2192 Number of Years Paid\": If > 1, the premium covers multiple years.\n- \"Health Insurance \u2192 Number of Years Paid\": If > 1, the premium covers multiple years.\n- \"Education Loan Interest \u2192 Year of Repayment\": The Nth year of the repayment schedule (e.g. 1 = first year, 5 = fifth year). This is NOT a calendar or fiscal year.\n- \"Held for duration in years\" (for Bonds, Debentures, G-Secs, Privately Owned Vehicle): Integer years the asset was held.\n- \"Health Insurance \u2192 Paid By\": \"self\" means the individual paid; \"group medical insurance\" means employer-provided coverage.\n- \"Stock Sale Transactions \u2192 STT\": Securities Transaction Tax paid on the transaction.\n- \"Long/Short Term Capital Loss \u2192 Financial Year\": The FY when the loss was originally incurred, in \"YYYY-YY\" format (e.g. \"2020-21\").\n- \"Mutual Fund Transactions \u2192 Type\": One of: equity, debt, elss, gold-etf, gold-mf, international, hybrid-equity.\n\n## Required output JSON schema\n\nYour response must be a single JSON object with exactly this structure and these exact key names. All values must be numbers. Do not add, remove, or rename any keys.\n\n{\n    \"Under Head Salaries\": {\n        \"Gross Salary\": 0,\n        \"Exemptions\": {\n            \"Section 10(13A)\": 0,\n            \"Section 10(5)\": 0\n        },\n        \"Section 16(ia)\": 0,\n        \"Section 16(ii)\": 0,\n        \"Section 16(iii)\": 0,\n        \"Net Salary\": 0\n    },\n    \"Capital Gains\": {\n        \"STCG (Section 111A)\": 0,\n        \"STCG (Other)\": {\n            \"Bonds\": 0,\n            \"Debentures\": 0,\n            \"G-Secs\": 0,\n            \"Mutual Funds\": 0,\n            \"Total\": 0\n        },\n        \"LTCG (Section 112A)\": 0,\n        \"LTCG (Non-Equity)\": {\n            \"Bonds\": 0,\n            \"Debentures\": 0,\n            \"G-Secs\": 0,\n            \"Mutual Funds\": 0,\n            \"Total\": 0\n        },\n        \"LTCG (Other)\": 0\n    },\n    \"Income from Other Sources\": {\n        \"Savings Bank Interest\": 0,\n        \"Deposit Interest\": 0,\n        \"Other Interest\": 0,\n        \"EPF Taxable Interest\": 0\n    },\n    \"Gross Total Income\": 0,\n    \"Deductions\": {\n        \"80C\": 0,\n        \"80CCC\": 0,\n        \"80CCD(1)\": 0,\n        \"80CCD(1B)\": 0,\n        \"80CCD(2)\": 0,\n        \"80D\": 0,\n        \"80E\": 0,\n        \"80G\": 0,\n        \"80TTA\": 0,\n        \"80TTB\": 0,\n        \"Total Deductions\": 0\n    },\n    \"Total Taxable Income\": 0,\n    \"Tax Computation\": {\n        \"Tax at Slab Rates\": 0,\n        \"Tax on STCG (Section 111A)\": 0,\n        \"Tax on STCG (Other)\": 0,\n        \"Tax on LTCG (Section 112A)\": 0,\n        \"Tax on LTCG (Non-Equity)\": 0,\n        \"Tax on LTCG (Other)\": 0,\n        \"Total Tax Before Rebate\": 0,\n        \"Less: Rebate under Section 87A\": 0,\n        \"Tax After Rebate\": 0,\n        \"Surcharge\": 0,\n        \"Health and Education Cess\": 0,\n        \"Total Tax Liability\": 0,\n        \"Less: TDS\": 0,\n        \"Net Tax Payable / Refund\": 0\n    }\n}\n\n## Response format rules\n\nIf you need to reason, do so inside <think></think> tags before the JSON. Your response after the closing </think> tag must be only the JSON object.\n\nDo not include any explanation after the closing }.\nDo not say \"Here is the JSON\" or anything similar before the {.\n\nWRONG: ```json\n{ ... }\n```\nCORRECT: { ... }\n\nYour entire response must be a single JSON object. Begin your response with { and end with }. Nothing else."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Here is the taxpayer input:\n{\n  \"Age\": 45,\n  \"Employment Type\": \"private\",\n  \"Tax Regime\": \"old\",\n  \"City\": \"metro\",\n  \"Gross Salary\": {\n    \"Basic Salary\": 3500000,\n    \"Dearness Allowance\": 500000,\n    \"HRA\": 800000,\n    \"Conveyance Allowance\": 80000,\n    \"Medical Allowance\": 50000,\n    \"Bonuses and Incentives\": 600000,\n    \"Overtime Pay\": 100000,\n    \"LTA\": 100000,\n    \"Special Allowance\": 4570000,\n    \"Entertainment Allowance\": 3000\n  },\n  \"Actual Rent Paid\": 2800000,\n  \"LTA Travel Expenses Claimed\": 50000,\n  \"Professional Tax\": 2500,\n  \"Stock Sale Transactions\": [\n    {\n      \"Sale Price\": 150,\n      \"Cost Price\": 200,\n      \"Quantity\": 1000,\n      \"Brokerage\": 500,\n      \"STT\": 250,\n      \"Purchase Date\": \"2025-04-01\",\n      \"Sale Date\": \"2025-10-15\",\n      \"FMV as of 31 Jan 2018\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"Long Term Capital Loss\": [\n    {\n      \"Financial Year\": \"2023-24\",\n      \"Loss Amount\": 50000\n    }\n  ],\n  \"Short Term Capital Loss\": [],\n  \"Mutual Fund Transactions\": [\n    {\n      \"Type\": \"elss\",\n      \"Purchase Date\": \"2022-01-01\",\n      \"Sale Date\": \"2025-06-01\",\n      \"Purchase Value\": 150000,\n      \"Sale Value\": 250000\n    },\n    {\n      \"Type\": \"international\",\n      \"Purchase Date\": \"2023-01-01\",\n      \"Sale Date\": \"2025-06-01\",\n      \"Purchase Value\": 150000,\n      \"Sale Value\": 200000\n    }\n  ],\n  \"Privately Owned Vehicle\": {\n    \"Sale Amount\": 0,\n    \"Purchase Amount\": 0,\n    \"Held for duration in years\": 0\n  },\n  \"Bonds\": {\n    \"Sale Amount\": 120000,\n    \"Purchase Amount\": 100000,\n    \"Held for duration in years\": 0.5\n  },\n  \"Debentures\": {\n    \"Sale Amount\": 0,\n    \"Purchase Amount\": 0,\n    \"Held for duration in years\": 0\n  },\n  \"G-Secs\": {\n    \"Sale Amount\": 0,\n    \"Purchase Amount\": 0,\n    \"Held for duration in years\": 0\n  },\n  \"Savings Bank Interest\": 25000,\n  \"Deposit Interest\": 30000,\n  \"Other Interest\": 5000,\n  \"EPF Taxable Interest\": 8000,\n  \"PPF\": 100000,\n  \"EPF\": {\n    \"Employee Contribution\": {\n      \"Deducted from Salary\": 0,\n      \"Voluntary\": 0\n    },\n    \"Employer Contribution\": 0\n  },\n  \"ELSS\": 80000,\n  \"NSC\": 0,\n  \"Sukanya Samriddhi Yojana\": 0,\n  \"SCSS\": 0,\n  \"Pension Scheme Premium\": {\n    \"Amount\": 60000,\n    \"Number of Years Paid\": 3\n  },\n  \"NPS\": {\n    \"Tier-1 Self Contribution\": 50000,\n    \"Tier-1 Employer Contribution\": 50000,\n    \"Tier-2\": 0\n  },\n  \"Education Loan Interest\": {\n    \"Interest Paid\": 80000,\n    \"Year of Repayment\": 5\n  },\n  \"Health Insurance\": [],\n  \"Donations\": [\n    {\n      \"Scheme Name\": \"PM Cares Fund\",\n      \"Amount\": 5000,\n      \"Mode\": \"cash\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"TDS\": 1761336.72\n}\n\nUse the calculate tool for ALL arithmetic \u2014 never perform mental math.\nBatch your calls: group independent calculations into the same response as several parallel calculate calls, rather than sending one at a time. Aim for roughly 5-10 calls per response \u2014 enough to make progress, but stop and wait for the results rather than trying to emit every remaining calculation at once.\nYou have a budget of 20 rounds, so a handful of moderate batches will comfortably cover a 37-field return. Once you have the numbers you need, output the final JSON."}, {"role": "assistant", "tool_calls": 3}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call-b12fd71f-87ef-4331-86f7-0829d6d0c270", "content": "10303000"}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call-3bb22e9b-f53d-49b8-b34c-9b2941164f0c", "content": "1050000"}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call-67e189cf-41fe-4eb3-8539-06cae70c9b1c", "content": "50000"}, {"role": "assistant", "tool_calls": 3}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call-5d529978-c2a5-4727-a53a-09998f8c7d22", "content": "4000000"}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call-c4771f36-3341-4a2e-b817-46e93586d936", "content": "2000000.0"}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call-9b3157aa-1137-47d2-8f1d-2650af343121", "content": "400000.0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I have:\n- Basic + DA = 4,000,000\n- 50% of (Basic + DA) = 2,000,000 (for metro)\n- 10% of (Basic + DA) = 400,000\n- Rent paid - 10% = 2,800,000 - 400,000 = 2,400,000\n\nHRA exemption = min(800,000, 2,400,000, 2,000,000) = 800,000\n\nLTA exemption = min(100,000, 50,000) = 50,000\n\nStandard deduction = 50,000\nProfessional tax = 2,500\nEntertainment allowance = 0 (private employee)\n\nNow let me calculate Net Salary:\nGross Salary = 10,303,000\nLess: HRA exemption = 800,000\nLess: LTA exemption = 50,000\nLess"}]}
